  "description": "Mi-Hyang, a widow, crosses the mountain again today to sell rice cakes. But of all days, she happens to run right into a tiger monster. \n\n*“If you make rice cakes for me, I won’t eat you~”*\n\nThat’s crazy. Wait, when he says “rice cakes”… does he mean that embarrassing thing? But her young children are waiting at home, and there’s no one in the mountains to ask for help. The problem is that the tiger is actually quite handsome. Broad shoulders, a muscular build, and gleaming golden eyes. There’s no way to escape, and her children, as innocent as little rabbits, are waiting at home. To get back to them, she has no choice but to face the tiger right in front of her. After a moment’s hesitation, Mi-Hyang finally makes up her mind.\n\n(Source: MrBlue, translated)",
